Isolith (Open Engineering Platform)
===================================
Copyright (c) 2026 Isolith contributors

Isolith is distributed under a per-crate hybrid licence. Two full licence
texts are included at the repository root:

  LICENSE-APACHE  Apache License, Version 2.0
  LICENSE-AGPL    GNU Affero General Public License, Version 3

Both texts are the unmodified canonical texts published by the Apache
Software Foundation and the Free Software Foundation respectively.

Which licence applies to which part of the code is a per-crate boundary, not
a prose statement. Every crate under crates/ declares its licence in its
Cargo.toml and is listed in the boundary map:

  docs/licensing-boundary.md   (human-readable)
  docs/licensing-boundary.json (machine-checkable)

The same rule, in one line: Apache-2.0 for applications and libraries;
AGPL-3.0 for the server, the PDM, and the P2P orchestration components.
The boundary map gives the licence and the reason for every crate, and
resolves the two boundary questions the line leaves open:

  - A library consumed by an AGPL component stays Apache-2.0 (the licence
    of a consumer does not change the licence of the consumed crate).
  - A shared contract crate takes the licence of the component it contracts:
    the P2P lane contract crates (oep-job, oep-state) are AGPL-3.0.

The boundary is enforced in CI by scripts/licensing-check.py, which fails
when a crate's declared licence disagrees with the map or when a dependency
introduces a licence outside the allow-list.

Third-party open-source components are listed in NOTICE. It is generated
from the committed Cargo.lock by scripts/licensing-check.py --regen and
verified in CI; do not edit it by hand.

Contributions are accepted under the Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO)
with no Contributor License Agreement; see CONTRIBUTING.md. Copyright
stays with each contributor; code is submitted under the licence of the
directory it lands in, as stated in this file.
